I also completed a second challenge:
Given a string, determine if it is a valid ISBN-13 number.

A valid ISBN-13:

 -Contains only digits and hyphens.
 -Has exactly 13 digits after removing hyphens.
 -Passes the following check: Multiply each digit by 1 or 3, alternating (multiply the first digit by 1, the second by 3, etc.). 
  The sum of the results must be divisible by 10.

First, I removed all hyphens using .replace(). 
Then, I checked if the length of the string was exactly 13. After that, I separated the characters into two variables: 
one that stores every other character and one that stores the remainder.
I implemented two for-loops to iterate over these variables, converting each character into an integer using int(). 
Then, I multiplied the numbers by either 1 or 3 and appended the results to two separate lists. Finally, I calculated the total sum and checked if it was divisible by 10.


